# Instructions
- Rank at most 5 priorities. Each cites at least one source, copied verbatim (type and ref) from the agent answers or the snapshot. Never invent a source.
- "objective" is the id of the brief objective the priority serves: one of o1, o2.
- At least one priority cites a declared north star as a path source (docs/vision.md). Cite only those as north stars.
- Keep everything under <out_of_scope> out of the priorities.
- "owner_role" is the id of the agent that proposed the priority most strongly, exactly as it heads its answer.
- "disagreements": only real conflicts between agents; an empty array when there are none. Each position's "role" is an agent id.
- "decisions": things that need the approval of Ada before anything changes. Each with its reason and an "action": what an agent would do after the approval, in one sentence. Each also lists in "priorities" the indexes (starting at 0, in the order of your "priorities") of the priorities it covers; an empty array when it covers none. Approving the decision marks those priorities accepted.
- "script": a team call in Spanish, written to be spoken, in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English style applied to Spanish: one topic in each sentence, at most 20 words in a sentence, the active voice with a named agent, simple verb forms, the condition first, one name for each thing. No slogans, metaphors, filler or fragments for effect. The pm opens by stating the question. Each agent that answered speaks its own view in 2 to 4 sentences, in first person. Refer to commits and files by what they are, never read hashes or paths aloud. Name a story by its title, never by its id. Add a short back-and-forth where agents disagree. The pm closes with the ranked priorities and the decisions Ada must take. Total about 2 to 4 minutes of speech. No markdown, no emojis. The "role" of each segment is the id of one of the agents that answered, or pm.
- Everything in Spanish except identifiers, paths and code.

